            <h1>Featured Projects</h1>
            <p style="color: #64748b;">A showcase of systems engineering, full-stack web applications, and database architectural solutions built during my academic and personal development.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="project-card">
            <div class="project-header">
                <span class="project-title">Blue River Zoo Management System</span>
                <span class="project-subtitle">Full-Stack Web Application</span>
            </div>
            
            <p class="project-desc">
                An interactive web-based facility management portal engineered for zoo operations. The system features multi-role access control tailored specifically for Visitors, Staff, and Administrators to streamline facility interactions, ticket scheduling, and animal care tracking.
            </p>

            <div class="project-highlights-title">Key Capabilities & Features:</div>
            <ul class="project-highlights">
                <li><strong>Role-Based Access Control:</strong> Distinct interfaces and privileges for Visitors (ticket bookings, schedules), Staff (daily duties, facility updates), and Admins (system reporting, user management).</li>
                <li><strong>Dynamic Frontend Interface:</strong> Responsive JavaScript UI components providing real-time interactive scheduling and user dashboards.</li>
                <li><strong>Relational SQL Backend:</strong> Designed a structured database backend to handle user authentication, booking transactions, and facility resource allocations efficiently.</li>
            </ul>

            <div class="tech-stack">
                <span class="tech-badge">C#</span>
                <span class="tech-badge">JavaScript</span>
                <span class="tech-badge">SQL Database</span>
                <span class="tech-badge">HTML/CSS</span>
                <span class="tech-badge">Web Facilities</span>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="project-card">
            <div class="project-header">
                <span class="project-title">MobiVet Mobile Veterinary Database System</span>
                <span class="project-subtitle">CMPG 311 Project</span>
            </div>

            <p class="project-desc">
                An end-to-end relational database solution designed to expand a primary clinic's operations into semi-independent mobile veterinary care units. Built to solve resource allocation conflicts, track fleet logistics, manage patient medical histories, and process service payments.
            </p>

            <div class="project-highlights-title">Key Architectural Highlights:</div>
            <ul class="project-highlights">
                <li><strong>Conflict Prevention & Business Rules:</strong> Designed data constraints to eliminate double-booking for shared veterinary staff, specialized vehicles, and home appointments.</li>
                <li><strong>Comprehensive Data Model:</strong> Conceptualized an ERD and Logical Schema covering 16 interrelated entities including Pet Owners, Patients, Appointments, Treatments, Vehicle Checklists, and Financial Payments.</li>
                <li><strong>Specialized Roles & Integrity Constraints:</strong> Implemented specialized supertype/subtype relationships for Staff roles (Veterinarians, Nurses, Drivers) and bridge entities for multi-service billing and staffing.</li>
            </ul>

            <div class="tech-stack">
                <span class="tech-badge">CMPG 311</span>
                <span class="tech-badge">Relational SQL</span>
                <span class="tech-badge">ERD Modeling</span>
                <span class="tech-badge">Logical Data Modeling</span>
                <span class="tech-badge">Integrity Constraints</span>
            </div>
        </div>

